    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "# METHOD 3: TOKEN-BASED SPLITTING\n",
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "# What: Splits text based on token count (not character count)\n",
    "# Why: LLMs have token limits (e.g., GPT-3.5 = 4096 tokens, GPT-4 = 8192 tokens)\n",
    "# When: When you need exact token counts for LLM API calls(TOKEN LIMITED MODELS)\n",
    "# How: Uses tokenizers to count tokens (tiktoken for OpenAI, etc.)\n",
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(\"METHOD 3: TOKEN TEXT SPLITTER\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "# WHY USE TOKEN-BASED SPLITTING?\n",
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "print(\"\\nWHY USE TOKEN-BASED SPLITTING?\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 80)\n",
    "print(\"\"\"\n",
    "1. LLMs have TOKEN LIMITS (not character limits):\n",
    "   → GPT-3.5: 4,096 tokens\n",
    "   → GPT-4:   8,192 tokens\n",
    "   → Claude:  100,000 tokens\n",
    "   → If you send more tokens, the API call fails!\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Different languages have DIFFERENT token counts:\n",
    "   → \"Hello\" = 1 token (English)\n",
    "   → \"你好\" = 2 tokens (Chinese - each character is a token)\n",
    "   → Character-based splitting doesn't account for this!\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Cost is based on TOKENS:\n",
    "   → OpenAI charges per 1,000 tokens\n",
    "   → Splitting by tokens helps control costs\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Token count ≠ Character count:\n",
    "   → 100 characters might be 20-30 tokens\n",
    "   → Depends on the language and tokenizer\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "# TOKEN TEXT SPLITTER\n",
