      "\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "TEXT SPLITTING METHODS COMPARISON\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "📝 CHARACTER TEXT SPLITTER\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "\n",
      "WHAT IT DOES:\n",
      "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
      "    │ Splits text based on a specific character          │\n",
      "    │ (space, comma, newline, etc.)                      │\n",
      "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
      "\n",
      "    Example with separator=\" \" (space):\n",
      "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
      "    │ \"Python is a powerful programming language\"            │\n",
      "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
      "                          ↓ SPLIT ON SPACES\n",
      "    ┌──────────┐ ┌────┐ ┌───┐ ┌─────────┐ ┌───────────┐ ┌───────┐\n",
      "    │ \"Python\" │ │\"is\"│ │\"a\"│ │\"powerful\"│ │\"programming\"│ │\"language\"│\n",
      "    └──────────┘ └────┘ └───┘ └─────────┘ └───────────┘ └───────┘\n",
      "    Then groups words until chunk_size is reached\n",
      "\n",
      "CHARACTERISTICS:\n",
      "    ✅ Simple and predictable\n",
      "    ✅ Fast processing\n",
      "    ✅ Easy to understand\n",
      "    ✅ Works with any text\n",
      "    ✅ Good for structured text (CSV, JSON, etc.)\n",
      "\n",
      "    ❌ May break mid-sentence\n",
      "    ❌ Doesn't respect natural language boundaries\n",
      "    ❌ Can split words in half\n",
      "    ❌ Poor for semantic meaning preservation\n",
      "\n",
      "BEST USE CASES:\n",
      "    → Splitting CSV files by commas\n",
      "    → Splitting JSON by newlines\n",
      "    → Splitting code by semicolons\n",
      "    → Simple text where structure is consistent\n",
      "    → When you need exact character control\n",
      "\n",
      "WHEN TO AVOID:\n",
      "    → Natural language text (articles, books)\n",
      "    → When you need semantic meaning\n",
      "    → When sentence boundaries matter\n",
      "    → For RAG applications (use Recursive instead)\n",
      "\n",
      "CODE EXAMPLE:\n",
      "    char_splitter = CharacterTextSplitter(\n",
      "        chunk_size=200,\n",
      "        chunk_overlap=20,\n",
      "        separator=\" \",          # Split on spaces\n",
      "        length_function=len\n",
      "    )\n",
      "    chunks = char_splitter.split_text(text)\n",
      "\n",
      "\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "📚 RECURSIVE CHARACTER TEXT SPLITTER (RECOMMENDED ⭐)\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "\n",
      "WHAT IT DOES:\n",
      "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
      "    │ Recursively tries different separators              │\n",
      "    │ in order: paragraphs → sentences → words → chars   │\n",
      "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
      "\n",
      "    Example: Tries separators in order:\n",
      "    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
      "    │ \"Python is powerful. It has simple syntax. It is popular.\"  │\n",
      "    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
      "         ↓ TRY 1: Split by paragraphs (\"\\n\\n\") - no paragraphs found\n",
      "         ↓ TRY 2: Split by sentences (\". \") - found! \n",
      "    ┌────────────────────┐ ┌─────────────────────────┐ ┌────────────────────┐\n",
      "    │ \"Python is powerful.\"│ │ \"It has simple syntax.\"│ │ \"It is popular.\"    │\n",
      "    └────────────────────┘ └─────────────────────────┘ └────────────────────┘\n",
      "    Then groups sentences until chunk_size is reached\n",
      "\n",
      "CHARACTERISTICS:\n",
      "    ✅ Respects text structure (paragraphs, sentences)\n",
      "    ✅ Tries multiple separators intelligently\n",
      "    ✅ Best general-purpose splitter\n",
      "    ✅ Preserves semantic meaning\n",
      "    ✅ Maintains natural language boundaries\n",
      "    ✅ Prevents splitting sentences in half\n",
      "    ✅ Recommended by LangChain documentation\n",
      "    ✅ Most popular for RAG applications\n",
      "\n",
      "    ❌ Slightly more complex to understand\n",
      "    ❌ A bit slower than character-based\n",
      "    ❌ Requires choosing separators order\n",
      "\n",
      "BEST USE CASES:\n",
      "    → Articles, books, and long documents (DEFAULT CHOICE)\n",
      "    → Text where semantic meaning matters\n",
      "    → RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) applications\n",
      "    → Question-answering systems\n",
      "    → Chatbots and conversational AI\n",
      "    → Document search and retrieval\n",
      "    → Knowledge base creation\n",
      "    → ANY natural language text!\n",
      "\n",
      "WHEN TO AVOID:\n",
      "    → Structured data (CSV, JSON) - use CharacterTextSplitter\n",
      "    → When you need exact token counts - use TokenTextSplitter\n",
      "\n",
      "CODE EXAMPLE:\n",
      "    recursive_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(\n",
      "        chunk_size=200,\n",
      "        chunk_overlap=20,\n",
      "        separators=[\n",
      "            \"\\n\\n\",    # 1st: Paragraphs\n",
      "            \"\\n\",       # 2nd: Lines  \n",
      "            \". \",        # 3rd: Sentences\n",
      "            \" \",         # 4th: Words\n",
      "            \"\"           # 5th: Characters (last resort)\n",
      "        ],\n",
      "        length_function=len\n",
      "    )\n",
      "    chunks = recursive_splitter.split_text(text)\n",
      "\n",
      "\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "🎯 TOKEN TEXT SPLITTER\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "\n",
      "WHAT IT DOES:\n",
      "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
      "    │ Splits text based on token count using a tokenizer  │\n",
      "    │ (tiktoken for OpenAI, transformers for HuggingFace) │\n",
      "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
      "\n",
      "    Example:\n",
      "    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
      "    │ \"Python is a powerful programming language\"                 │\n",
      "    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
      "                          ↓ TOKENIZATION\n",
      "    ┌──────┐ ┌────┐ ┌───┐ ┌────────┐ ┌───────────┐ ┌────────┐\n",
      "    │Python│ │ is │ │ a │ │powerful│ │programming│ │language│\n",
      "    └──────┘ └────┘ └───┘ └────────┘ └───────────┘ └────────┘\n",
      "    [Token1] [Token2] [Token3] [Token4] [Token5] [Token6]\n",
      "                    ↓ GROUP UNTIL 50 TOKENS\n",
      "    [Chunk 1: 50 tokens] [Chunk 2: 50 tokens] [Chunk 3: 50 tokens]\n",
      "\n",
      "CHARACTERISTICS:\n",
      "    ✅ Respects model token limits (most important!)\n",
      "    ✅ More accurate for embeddings\n",
      "    ✅ Predictable API costs (cost = tokens)\n",
      "    ✅ Works consistently across languages\n",
      "    ✅ No risk of exceeding context window\n",
      "    ✅ Safe for production use\n",
      "    ✅ Handles different languages properly\n",
      "    ✅ Most accurate for LLM integration\n",
      "\n",
      "    ❌ Slower than character-based (requires tokenizer)\n",
      "    ❌ Requires additional dependencies (tiktoken)\n",
      "    ❌ Different tokenizers give different results\n",
      "    ❌ Harder to predict character length\n",
      "    ❌ More complex to configure\n",
      "\n",
      "BEST USE CASES:\n",
      "    → Working with token-limited models (GPT, Claude, etc.)\n",
      "    → When you know your target LLM\n",
      "    → Production applications with cost constraints\n",
      "    → Multi-language applications\n",
      "    → When you need exact token counts\n",
      "    → OpenAI API calls\n",
      "    → Fine-tuning and training\n",
      "    → Batch processing with cost optimization\n",
      "\n",
      "WHEN TO AVOID:\n",
      "    → When you don't know your target LLM\n",
      "    → When speed is critical (use CharacterTextSplitter)\n",
      "    → When working offline without internet\n",
      "\n",
      "CODE EXAMPLE:\n",
      "    token_splitter = TokenTextSplitter(\n",
      "        chunk_size=50,     # 50 tokens per chunk\n",
      "        chunk_overlap=10   # 10 tokens overlap\n",
      "    )\n",
      "    chunks = token_splitter.split_text(text)\n",
      "\n",
